      "content": "No, the DNS protocol itself is robust and reliable; there is no mechanism designed to make records randomly disappear or change unexpectedly. What you might be perceiving as \"active blocking\" or unpredictable behavior is likely the result of interacting with private DNS caches on your home router or ISP's infrastructure, which can inadvertently prioritize inconsistent responses to confuse the situation. To verify this, clearing the DNS cache locally and using an external diagnostic tool that bypasses your ISP would confirm the data is reaching the servers correctly without being tampered with.",
